Author:     cp <cpizzle1983@duck.com>
AuthorDate: Thu Jul 16 11:32:20 2026 +0200
Commit:     kaie@kuix.de <kaie@kuix.de>
CommitDate: Thu Jul 16 09:42:34 2026 +0000

    Bug 2051453 - Record alarm acknowledgements locally so a CalDAV ack-strip no longer over-suppresses future occurrences. r=tobyp

    IgnoredAlarmsStore exists so that dismissed alarms on servers that quietly
    discard our X-MOZ-LASTACK changes (e.g. Google) do not re-appear. It keyed
    the ignore list on the parent item's hashId and addAlarmsForItem() early
    returned for the whole item, so dismissing a single occurrence of a
    recurring event permanently suppressed every future occurrence: neither the
    alarm nor the notification ever fired again.

    Record the acknowledgement time alongside the hashId and, when deciding
    whether a past alarm was already acknowledged, use the most recent of that
    time and the parent item's alarmLastAck. A dismiss made offline is only
    recorded locally and can be newer than a server-persisted alarmLastAck, so
    taking the later of the two keeps it honoured. Only alarms at or before that
    time are suppressed, so the dismissed occurrence stays dismissed while future
    occurrences continue to fire. Legacy entries stored without a time keep the
    previous blanket behaviour.

    Also add a one-time migration that drops those pre-existing legacy entries
    (stored without an ack time) so already-suppressed items re-arm. It runs only
    when calendar.alarms.showmissed is false so it cannot surface a burst of past
    alarms; ack-bearing entries are left untouched.

    Adds test_dismissKeepsFutureOccurrencesArmed, test_newerLocalAckWinsOverServerAck,
    test_migrateClearsOnlyLegacyIgnoredEntries and test_migrateSkipsClearWhenShowMissedTrue.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311586

